    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n9310" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">com-mĕābĭlis</span></b> ,
			e, adj. (perh. only in Arn.). <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>Pass.</i>, <i>that is casily passed
				through</i>, 
			
			<i>permeable</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">venae,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Arn. 2, p. 84, 3</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<i>Act.</i>, <i>that easily passes
				through</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">aurae,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Arn. 7, p. 233</span></i>
			.</div>
